# Local design-tooling scratch: generated mockups, prompts and critiques. 4.8 MB of AI
# output that describes the console rather than being part of it, and it regenerates on
# demand — it was committed by an over-broad `git add -A`, not by intent.
.impeccable/
# Same tool, same accident. PRODUCT.md carries an `impeccable:product-schema` marker and is
# rewritten by the design skill, so tracking it means a diff on every design pass describing
# the product rather than changing it. The README is the durable answer to "what is this".
PRODUCT.md

# Review agents write throwaway probe suites here while a workflow runs, and a `git add -A` in
# that window sweeps them into a commit -- which is exactly how one reached main. Ignoring the
# prefix is a backstop, not the fix: the fix is staging paths instead of -A. Named `zz-` so they
# sort last and are obvious in a listing.
tests/zz-*.test.ts
.env*
